.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH record 1  "record " 
.SH NAME
record \- Record a shell session as a snippet
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrecord\fR [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-tags\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-push\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Record a shell session as a snippet
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
Short description
.TP
\fB\-\-tags\fR \fI<TAGS>\fR
Comma\-separated tags
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing snippet with the same name
.TP
\fB\-\-push\fR
After saving, offer to push to the cloud (when logged in)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
Name for the snippet (prompted when omitted)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fg record ubuntu\-setup \-\-description \*(AqBase packages\*(Aq \-\-tags ubuntu,setup
